      "body": "## Motivation\n`SchedulerReqTimeStats.__getstate__` returns `{}` unless metrics are enabled or the object carries timing data. Every `BatchTokenIDOutput` still ships one per request anyway. The detokenizer and the `TokenizerManager` then rebuild each of those empty objects through Python `__setstate__`, once per request per step. With metrics off (the default), that is per-token work on the tokenizer manager's event loop.\n\n## Modifications\n- `_GenerationStreamAccumulator` records whether any accepted request's time stats carry data, and sends `time_stats=None` otherwise. Every consumer already handles `None`: the tokenizer manager's metrics and first-token paths, the detokenizer passthrough, and the multi-tokenizer router.\n- `SchedulerReqTimeStats.has_wire_state()` is now the single condition used by both `__getstate__` and the accumulator.\n\nWhen metrics are on, nothing changes.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nN/A. Model outputs are unchanged.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\nSetup:\n- `sgl.Engine` with default flags (detokenizer on, metrics off).\n- The scheduler process is replaced by a GPU-free stand-in that emits real `BatchTokenIDOutput` messages. The `TokenizerManager` and detokenizer are unmodified.\n- Grace CPU (GB200 node), Python 3.12, 128 input / 1024 output tokens, one token per 8 ms per request, 1024 concurrent streams.\n\n| | Output tok/s (2 runs) | Tokenizer-manager main thread, µs/token |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| main | 64.6k / 65.0k | 15.4 |\n| this PR | 87.1k / 87.0k (**+34–35%**) | 10.9 |\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38482225732](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38482225732)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38482225592](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38482225592)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38482225740](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38482225740)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
